# History Around Town

**Signature editorial feature.** Replaces Bandit's Notebook. Final section of every homepage edition.

## Mission

An editorial collection of places that tell the story of a community — not a tourism guide, not an attraction list.

Subtitle (locked): **"Every town has a story waiting to be explored."**

## Tone

Timeless · calm · educational · beautifully written · premium local magazine

## Architecture (non-negotiable)

Same philosophy as Masterpiece Library:

1. Prepare each place **once** in `kindred_history_places`
2. Edition build copies frozen snapshot to `editions.history_around_town`
3. Client reads snapshot only — **no runtime AI, research, or generation**

## Homepage

- **Position:** always last section before edition close — never reorder other sections
- **Carousel:** ~20 curated cards (image, category, place name, teaser)
- **See All:** full vertical directory — **no artificial limit** (Gilbert 25, Seattle 120, DC 300+)

## What qualifies

Genuine places with historical, cultural, architectural, scientific, civic, or local significance:

Historic districts · homes · museums · monuments · memorials · courthouses · churches · schools · train depots · bridges · military sites · archaeological sites · cemeteries · neighborhoods · observatories · lighthouses · historically significant public art · hidden local landmarks

Do **not** limit to famous tourist attractions.

## Full article sections

History · Why it Matters · Interesting Facts · Architecture (when applicable) · Best Time to Visit · Hours · Admission · Parking · Accessibility · Open in Maps · Official Website · Nearby Places · Editorial Closing Note

## Publication gates

Every place must pass:

1. **Accuracy Test** — verified facts only
2. **Swap Test** — original closing belonging only to this place
3. **Lasting Thought Test** — one memorable idea
4. **Validation gate** — `validation_status = 'approved'`

## Images — NO AI (permanent law)

**Never use AI-generated images.** Every image must be authentic and verifiable.

Approved sources: official city/government sites · historical societies · museums · libraries/archives · Wikimedia Commons · verified Open Access collections · official landmark sites · properly licensed documentary photography.

Allowed types: authentic present-day photos · historical photographs · archival maps · historical illustrations · architectural drawings · public-domain documents · verified artwork tied to the location.

Never use: AI-generated or AI-enhanced fictional reconstructions · stock pretending to be the location · generic filler · unverified social media · wrong-location photos · fabricated historical scenes.

Every library record stores permanently: `image_url`/`hosted_url` · `image_source_url` · `image_credit` · `image_photographer` · `image_license` · `image_era` (`historical`|`present_day`) · `image_date` when known.

If no authentic image can be verified → `needs_review`. **HTTP 429 from Wikimedia → `verification_pending_rate_limit` — never reject the record.**

Image HTTP verification: `scripts/lib/historyPlaceImageVerification.mjs` — 3 retries with exponential backoff for trusted sources; 404/410 = failed only.

